<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland's ESB awarded 5.7 mln punts Ghana contract.</title>
<headline>Ireland's ESB awarded 5.7 mln punts Ghana contract.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>ESB International, an independent subsidiary of Ireland's Electricity Supply Board (ESB), has been awarded a 5.7 million punt three-year contract to manage and operate a power station in Ghana, Irish media said on Monday.</p>
<p>ESB International, which has had a base in the African country since 1985, said in a statement that it would also provide training services as part of the deal.</p>
<p>--Dublin newsroom 353-1-661-3377</p>
</text>
